' Target-only adaptation: current Runtime event wrapper, ordered content, eventId/sourceEventId and data-only SSE.
' Design reason: acknowledge durable Channel acceptance first; keep Chat ownership and persist the Runtime receipt before projection.
' Security hardening: no automatic replay after lost or unsaved acceptance receipts; recovery is shown in the state diagram.
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
hide footbox
skinparam maxMessageSize 170
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #64748B
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBorderColor #CBD5E1
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}
title Feishu Message - Durable Admission to Visible Reply
participant "Feishu Platform" as Feishu
participant "Adapter /\nInbound Service" as Inbound
database "Channel Store" as Store
participant "Execution Worker" as Worker
participant "Chat Core /\nRuntime Client" as Chat
participant "CampusClaw Runtime" as Runtime
participant "Projector /\nMessage Gateway" as Outbound

== 1. Accept durably ==
Feishu -> Inbound : Deliver message
Inbound -> Inbound : Verify and normalize
Inbound -> Store : Dedupe + Inbox + Outbox\nOne transaction
Store --> Inbound : Durable receipt
Inbound --> Feishu : Acknowledge delivery
break Duplicate provider message
  Inbound -> Inbound : Keep existing receipt
end

== 2. Bind and submit once ==
Worker -> Store : Claim FIFO task with fence
Store --> Worker : Message and lease
Worker -> Chat : Ensure dedicated Chat / Session
Chat -> Runtime : Create Session if absent
Runtime --> Chat : Session identity
Chat --> Worker : Persisted mapping
Worker -> Store : Save SUBMITTING and correlation
Store --> Worker : Commit
Worker -> Chat : Submit normalized content
Chat -> Runtime : POST event: user.message\nwith ordered content
Runtime --> Chat : data: full user.message\neventId
Chat --> Worker : Complete receipt
Worker -> Store : Save accepted_event_id\nClear content ciphertext atomically
Store --> Worker : Commit

== 3. Project and deliver ==
loop Live response before corresponding session.status_idle
  Runtime --> Chat : data: preview or complete event\nsourceEventId links original message
  Chat --> Worker : ChannelChatEventDTO
  Worker -> Outbound : Project allowed Assistant text
  Outbound -> Store : Save desired view + Outbox
  Store --> Outbound : Versioned delivery task
  Outbound -> Store : Save uuid / sequence before call
  Store --> Outbound : Commit
  Outbound -> Feishu : Create or update fixed card
  Feishu --> Outbound : Delivery result
end
Runtime --> Chat : data: corresponding session.status_idle
Chat --> Worker : Correlated reason
alt done / failed / terminated
  Worker -> Store : Save result + final projection task
  Store --> Outbound : Finalize card
  Outbound -> Feishu : Final text; close streaming mode
  Feishu --> Outbound : Delivery result
else confirming
  Worker -> Store : Keep execution active\nObserve full history; do not resubmit
  Store --> Worker : Waiting state saved
end
note over Worker,Runtime
confirming is a running wait, never success.
No Feishu confirmation entry exists in v1; constrain tools before launch.
Disconnect recovery depends on a saved receipt; see the recovery state diagram.
end note
@enduml

@startuml channel_feishu_recovery_state
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@1f801dbb82bdda30478e3354e685e3153b179a0c modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/UserEventAcceptance.java lines 17-25
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@1f801dbb82bdda30478e3354e685e3153b179a0c modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeExecutionCoordinator.java lines 68-82 and 150-164

' Observed behavior at fixed Java baseline: acceptance persists before execution; disconnect does not undo acceptance.
' Target-only adaptation: current complete Runtime events identify acceptance and causality via eventId/sourceEventId.
' Security hardening: missing receipt, empty history, matching text or idle state cannot prove non-acceptance.
' Design reason: the current POST has no business idempotency key; retry only an explicit not-accepted error.
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #64748B
}
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 40
title Channel Execution - Acceptance Determines Recovery
state "Saved Runtime receipt" as Observed {
  state STREAMING
  state RECONCILING
  STREAMING --> RECONCILING : Disconnect / restart /\nconfirming wait
  RECONCILING --> RECONCILING : Read full history pages
}
[*] --> ACCEPTED : Inbox + Outbox committed
ACCEPTED --> READY_TO_SUBMIT : FIFO lease acquired
READY_TO_SUBMIT --> SUBMITTING : Persist local correlation
SUBMITTING --> STREAMING : Save accepted_event_id\nand clear content
SUBMITTING --> READY_TO_SUBMIT : Not accepted:\nretryable error
SUBMITTING --> FAILED : Not accepted:\npermanent error
SUBMITTING --> MANUAL_RECONCILIATION : Receipt lost or not saved
Observed --> COMPLETED : Correlated terminal: done
Observed --> FAILED : Correlated terminal:\nfailed / terminated
RECONCILING --> MANUAL_RECONCILIATION : Ambiguous writer / branch /\nhistory / ownership
MANUAL_RECONCILIATION --> COMPLETED : Verified outcome
MANUAL_RECONCILIATION --> FAILED : Unresolved outcome
COMPLETED --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]
legend bottom left
RECONCILING matches eventId / sourceEventId in full history; it never POSTs again.
Only the corresponding session.status_idle gives a terminal execution result.
Idle alone, empty history and equal text are not acceptance or completion evidence.
Fencing coordinates Channel workers; an expired lease does not stop old Runtime work.
Delivery retries reuse the stored uuid and sequence; permanent delivery errors dead-letter.
endlegend
@enduml
